[1355.978782, "o", "[09:27:19] ✅ Complete env_variable_shadowing_astronomy_shop: results={'Diagnosis': {'judgment': 'False', 'reasoning': 'Verdict: main.py:664\r\n           False (composite=0.45). D1 Fault Localization: 0.67 | D2 Fault Characterization: 0.00 | D3 Scope Precision: 0.67.                \r\n           Weakest dimension: Fault Characterization (0.00). Checklist details: [{\"id\": \"D1-Q1\", \"answer\": \"Yes\", \"evidence\":               \r\n           \"Faulty component: `frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` (container **frontend\\\\u2011proxy**)\", \"confidence\": \"High\"},                \r\n           {\"id\": \"D1-Q2\", \"answer\": \"No\", \"evidence\": \"Diagnosis cites memory\\\\u2011limit OOM as cause, while                              \r\n           ground\\\\u2011truth cites duplicate `FRONTEND_HOST` env var\", \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D1-Q3\", \"answer\": \"Yes\",             \r\n           \"evidence\": \"Diagnosis identifies `frontend-proxy` as the faulty component, matching ground\\\\u2011truth component\",              \r\n           \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D2-Q1\", \"answer\": \"No\", \"evidence\": \"Diagnosis mentions memory limit OOM, not the                 \r\n           duplicate env\\\\u2011var mechanism\", \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D2-Q2\", \"answer\": \"No\", \"evidence\": \"No mention of            \r\n           `FRONTEND_HOST` env var or its duplicated values\", \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D2-Q3\", \"answer\": \"No\", \"evidence\":            \r\n           \"Diagnosis attributes fault to memory limit, an unrelated fault type\", \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D3-Q1\",                    \r\n           \"answer\": \"Yes\", \"evidence\": \"Only `frontend-proxy` is blamed; other pods are listed as healthy\", \"confidence\":                  \r\n           \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D3-Q2\", \"answer\": \"Yes\", \"evidence\": \"Diagnosis includes the `frontend-proxy` component, the sole               \r\n           component in ground\\\\u2011truth\", \"confidence\": \"High\"}, {\"id\": \"D3-Q3\", \"answer\": \"No\", \"evidence\": \"Diagnosis                  \r\n           describes OOM\\\\u2011kill outage, whereas ground\\\\u2011truth describes wrong upstream routing while pod stays Ready\",             \r\n           \"confidence\": \"High\"}]', 'success': False, 'accuracy': 45.0, 'composite_score': 0.45, 'dimensions': {'D1': {'name':              \r\n           'Fault Localization', 'score': 0.67}, 'D2': {'name': 'Fault Characterization', 'score': 0.0}, 'D3': {'name': 'Scope              \r\n           Precision', 'score': 0.67}}, 'checklist': [{'id': 'D1-Q1', 'answer': 'Yes', 'evidence': 'Faulty component:                       \r\n           `frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` (container **frontend‑proxy**)', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D1-Q2', 'answer':               \r\n           'No', 'evidence': 'Diagnosis cites memory‑limit OOM as cause, while ground‑truth cites duplicate `FRONTEND_HOST` env             \r\n           var', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D1-Q3', 'answer': 'Yes', 'evidence': 'Diagnosis identifies `frontend-proxy` as              \r\n           the faulty component, matching ground‑truth component', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D2-Q1', 'answer': 'No',                   \r\n           'evidence': 'Diagnosis mentions memory limit OOM, not the duplicate env‑var mechanism', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id':            \r\n           'D2-Q2', 'answer': 'No', 'evidence': 'No mention of `FRONTEND_HOST` env var or its duplicated values', 'confidence':             \r\n           'High'}, {'id': 'D2-Q3', 'answer': 'No', 'evidence': 'Diagnosis attributes fault to memory limit, an unrelated fault             \r\n           type', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D3-Q1', 'answer': 'Yes', 'evidence': 'Only `frontend-proxy` is blamed; other               \r\n           pods are listed as healthy', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D3-Q2', 'answer': 'Yes', 'evidence': 'Diagnosis includes             \r\n           the `frontend-proxy` component, the sole component in ground‑truth', 'confidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D3-Q3', 'answer':            \r\n           'No', 'evidence': 'Diagnosis describes OOM‑kill outage, whereas ground‑truth describes wrong upstream routing while              \r\n           pod stays Ready', 'confidence': 'High'}], 'submission': '**Investigation Summary**\\n\\n| Entity | Kind | Namespace |              \r\n           Status / Reason | Evidence |\\n|--------|------|------------|-----------------|----------|\\n|                                     \r\n           `frontend‑proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` | Pod | astronomy‑shop | **Running** but **Ready\\u202f=\\u202ffalse**; container                 \r\n           terminated with **OOMKilled** (exit\\u202fcode\\u202f137) – 4 restarts | `kubectl describe pod …` shows `State:                    \r\n           Terminated – Reason: OOMKilled`, `Restart Count: 4`, `Limits: memory\\u202f65Mi` |\\n| All other pods (27 total) | Pod             \r\n           | astronomy‑shop | **Running / Ready\\u202f=\\u202ftrue** | `kubectl_tabular_query` shows `READY: true` for every pod              \r\n           except the frontend‑proxy |\\n| Alert `KubePodNotReady` | Prometheus alert | astronomy‑shop | **Firing** – pod not                \r\n           ready >\\u202f1\\u202fmin | `get_alerts` returned alert with `pod: frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` |\\n| Node                       \r\n           `kind‑worker3` | Node | – | **Healthy** (CPU\\u202f≈\\u202f1\\u202f%, Memory\\u202f≈\\u202f9\\u202f%) | `kubectl_top_nodes`            \r\n           |\\n\\n**Root Cause**\\n\\n- **Faulty component:** `frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` (container **frontend‑proxy**)  \\n-              \r\n           **Misconfiguration:** Memory limit set to **65\\u202fMiB** (`Limits: memory: 65Mi`). The proxy process exceeds this               \r\n           limit, causing the container to be **OOMKilled** repeatedly (restart count\\u202f=\\u202f4) and entering a back‑off                \r\n           state.  \\n- **Why it breaks the app:** The frontend‑proxy routes traffic to all other services. When it is OOM‑killed            \r\n           and not ready, the UI cannot reach downstream services, resulting in a complete outage for the shop front‑end.                   \r\n           \\n\\n**Evidence**\\n\\n1. `kubectl describe pod` – shows `State: Terminated – Reason: OOMKilled`, `Exit Code: 137`,                 \r\n           `Restart Count: 4`, `Limits: memory: 65Mi`.  \\n2. Pod events include `Warning BackOff` for the container.  \\n3.                  \r\n           Prometheus alert `KubePodNotReady` firing for this pod.  \\n4. All other pods are running and ready, confirming the               \r\n           issue is isolated to the frontend‑proxy.  \\n\\n**Remediation**\\n\\n1. **Increase memory resources** for the                        \r\n           `frontend-proxy` container (e.g., `requests: 128Mi`, `limits: 256Mi`).  \\n2. Apply the change via the Helm chart (or             \r\n           Deployment manifest) and roll out the update:  \\n   ```bash\\n   helm upgrade astronomy-shop ./chart \\\\\\n     --set               \r\n           frontendProxy.resources.limits.memory=256Mi \\\\\\n     --set frontendProxy.resources.requests.memory=128Mi \\\\\\n     -n             \r\n           astronomy-shop\\n   ```\\n3. Verify the pod becomes Ready and the alert clears:  \\n   ```bash\\n   kubectl wait                     \r\n           --for=condition=Ready pod -l app.kubernetes.io/name=frontend-proxy -n astronomy-shop --timeout=2m\\n   ```\\n4. Monitor            \r\n"]
[1355.978863, "o", "           the pod’s memory usage (`kubectl top pod frontend-proxy-…`) to ensure the new limits are sufficient.                             \r\n           \\n\\n**Impact**\\n\\n- **Affected:** `frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-jsr6n` (OOMKilled, not ready).  \\n- **Checked, healthy:**            \r\n           All other 26 pods in the `astronomy-shop` namespace.  \\n- **Changed for another reason:** None observed.  \\n\\nAfter              \r\n           increasing the memory limits and confirming the pod stabilises, the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop should resume              \r\n           normal operation.'}, 'TTL': 200.83027529716492, 'phase.fix_kubernetes.duration_s': 3.438,                                        \r\n           'phase.undeploy_leftovers.duration_s': 6.168, 'phase.deploy.duration_s': 615.77, 'phase.inject_fault.duration_s':                \r\n           9.28, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.duration_s': 156.718, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.outcome': 'submitted',                                 \r\n           'phase.evaluate:diagnosis.duration_s': 43.654, 'phase.cleanup.duration_s': 147.545, 'run_status': 'complete'}                    \r\n"]
